===East Germany vs Australia===
This was the first ever fixture in the World Cup finals for Australia, with one West German newspaper labelling the team as “no-hope” Australians, and later printing an apology.<ref >{{Cite web |website=Socceroos |date=25 July 2012 |title=Green and Golden years – The ’74 Socceroos v East Germany |url=https://socceroos.com.au/news/green-and-golden-years-74-socceroos-v-east-germany}}</ref>

Australia kept the highly-fancied East German side scoreless until the second half, when Australia defender [[Colin Curran]] deflected the ball into his own team's net, making unwanted history by being the first Australia player in the World Cup to score a goal, albeit an [[own goal]].<ref >{{Cite web |website=Socceroos |date=11 April 2018 |title=Col Curran's FIFA World Cup story |url=https://socceroos.com.au/news/67-days-go-col-currans-fifa-world-cup-story}}</ref> East Germany forward [[Joachim Streich]] scored half-way through the second half, securing the 2–0 victory for East Germany.
