===Australia vs Chile===
The fixture was played during a torrential downpour, necessitating the half-time break to be extended by 22 minutes.<ref >{{Cite web |website=Herald Sun|last=Hinds |first=Richard |date=10 June 2014 |title=Australia faced Chile at the 1974 World Cup, drawing 0-0 after losses to East and West Germany |url=https://www.heraldsun.com.au/sport/football/world-cup/australia-faced-chile-at-the-1974-world-cup-drawing-00-after-losses-to-east-and-west-germany/news-story/4c2271bffe6cd6d641e067161f989308}}</ref>

[[Ray Richards (footballer)|Ray Richards]] received a second booking late in the second half for not taking a freekick quickly enough, however he was allowed to stay on the pitch due to the referee forgetting about his first booking.<ref name="rayrichardsSbs">{{Cite web |website=SBS Sport|last=Micallef |first=Philip |date=18 December 2018 |title=Socceroos Greats - Where are they now: Ray Richards |url=https://www.sbs.com.au/sport/article/socceroos-greats-where-are-they-now-ray-richards/ge80tt6zb}}</ref> He remained on the pitch for several minutes before the linesman alerted the referee about his mistake, resulting in the referee showing him a third yellow, followed by the required red card.<ref name="rayrichardsSbs"/> Richards became the first Australia player to be sent off in a World Cup game.<ref >{{Cite web |website=Socceroos.com.au |date=11 April 2018 |title=Ray Richards' FIFA World Cup story |url=https://socceroos.com.au/news/66-days-go-ray-richards-fifa-world-cup-story}}</ref> Coincidentally, a similar incident occurred involving Australia when they returned to the World Cup in Germany over three decades later in [[2006 FIFA World Cup|2006]] against Croatia - in this case, [[List of 2006 FIFA World Cup controversies#Three yellow cards|Josip Šimunić was erroneously shown three yellow cards before being sent off by referee Graham Poll]].

This result earned Australia their first ever point and clean sheet at the World Cup finals.<ref >{{Cite web |last=Gorman |first=Joe |website=The Guardian |date=11 June 2014 |quote=That 0-0 draw between Chile and Australia in Berlin in June 1974 is the Socceroos' first point at a World Cup|title=Socceroos v Chile World Cup match recalls a painful history |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/blog/2014/jun/11/socceroos-chile-world-cup-2014}}</ref>
